From 597f177b59fd1555415631b549ca89a111dc7de6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:01:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 101/106] drm/evdi: add the Rust virtual display driver

Add a Rust implementation of EVDI while preserving the established
libevdi and DisplayLinkManager display ABI. Install that ABI as
a normal DRM UAPI header, use generated Rust UAPI bindings, and
translate its pointer-bearing ioctls for 32-bit clients.

Create cards through the established platform sysfs interface and
expose the expected DRM ioctls and events. Use owned DRM, KMS, event,
framebuffer, and sysfs abstractions throughout.

Prepare a bounded four-entry scanout pool with owned shmem mappings so
compositor swapchain buffers are mapped before notifying the client and
reused for later flips and GRABPIX calls. Enforce the bandwidth limits
supplied by userspace without applying a driver-invented multiplier.

DDC/CI and cursor-control ioctls remain ABI-compatible no-ops. The
driver advertises no cursor plane and does not register a virtual
I2C adapter.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
